Assistant B has a stronger architectural outline, but its implementation has more serious functional problems. Most importantly, `stopRecording` returns a hard-coded placeholder URL instead of the actual recording URL. It also does not request microphone permission, and its visualizer uses simulated volume rather than audio levels, so it does not show the user’s voice input. Its timer is not invalidated, and the audio session is configured and activated during service initialization rather than as part of a permission-aware recording flow.

